{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:07:49.158978Z","id":"370cdcd3887110f51895282eee93acc893f02cf7243eb67dde321aa956824b5a","body":{"detail":"Embed::open starts the core with require_credential: true (spec §2.3), and a shell-page frame carries no credential (spec §2.3 table; crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs request() drops authorization and cookie for it). clax_http::auth::require_credential (crates/clax-http/src/auth.rs:347-363) lets through only open_without_credential's paths (/healthz, /_clax/, /c/, /_blob/; auth.rs:332-337), so GET /a/<id>?app=1 and /assets/... as shell-page answer 401 unauthorized. Probed through Embed::call on a fresh home: '/a/<id>?app=1 -> 401 {\"error\":{\"code\":\"unauthorized\",...}}', '/_clax/bridge.js -> 200', '/c/<id>/v/1/ -> 200'. The daemon app avoided this with the clax_key_<port> cookie, which also made the shell document's boot data the owner's (shell/boot.rs assemble: who.is_owner()). Options: (a) the core adds the owner's credential to shell-page frames, since the host sends them only for the shell origin's main-frame navigation and its subresources (spec §4.2), keeping today's owner boot data; (b) open_without_credential admits /a/, /assets/ and /favicon.ico when AppState.embed is set, and the shell document's boot is a visitor's until the shell fetches over ClaxHost; (c) the core runs without require_credential, as nothing but the app can reach it (spec §4.3, no port). Phase 1's tests do not load the shell document; Tasks 14 and 15 (the scheme handlers and the host relay) need one of these.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":368},"end":{"line":373},"content_hash":"4dd88cffd385f2ccccb1be4ffa321d6c52b08921f2ac3b9e0586670160aa9616"},"summary":"A shell-page frame for the shell document or its assets answers 401 under the core's require_credential, so the app's WebView cannot load the shell as spec 2026-10-19 §2.3 frames it","tags":["status:needs-decision","embed","security","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:24:57.700310Z","id":"353a5bfe8ab3936b81f89d5a19b076c84ec473e51cd0908ef623dac33f2f91fb","body":{"detail":"ffi_open passes OpenOptions.log: None, since clax_embed_open (include/clax_embed.h) takes only the home, and spec 2026-10-19 §2.1 lists src/log.rs (the rolling log moved from clax-ios, which logged to <cache>/daemon.log) without saying where its path comes from. The app's core therefore logs nowhere. A path in <home>/embed.json beside the origins, or a fixed <home>/logs/core.log, would need the spec to say which.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":104},"end":{"line":104},"content_hash":"9d27fbc89fbf57016f3423d76cc5d0a2b41e8c1d537a59a2fdc934be680fb49d"},"summary":"A core opened through clax_embed_open writes no log: the C ABI names no log path","tags":["embed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/ffi.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:42:06.460565Z","id":"bd6b5f9640c3e876bea9f1de062e9cd505d412e37779ce4e87314bcc08d38441","body":{"detail":"std::slice::from_raw_parts requires a non-null, aligned pointer even when the length is 0; a Dart caller that passes `nullptr` for an empty home or frame (or `malloc<Uint8>(0)`, which may return NULL) is undefined behaviour in release builds and an abort from the debug UB check in debug ones. `ClaxPost` is `extern \"C\" fn`, which Rust assumes is never NULL; a NULL `post` is UB the moment clax_embed_open is entered. include/clax_embed.h states neither pointer must be non-NULL, and the SAFETY comments (ffi.rs:22, :41) claim only readability. Task 12's Dart bindings are not written yet, so the contract can still be fixed on either side.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":14},"end":{"line":44},"content_hash":"9cc8c54b80ef001b5ed7b01ff828e177d71a82e726db829af413c1121868fc66"},"suggested_fix":"State in include/clax_embed.h that `home`, `req` and `post` are never NULL (and `home_len`/`req_len` > 0), and in the safe code before each SAFETY line return 0 / 2 when the pointer `is_null()`; the unsafe check allows safe lines there.","summary":"clax_embed_open and clax_embed_call make a slice of a pointer that may be NULL, and take `post` as a non-nullable function pointer: UB for a NULL from the caller","tags":["review","ffi","embed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:42:06.460634Z","id":"88445919da55cd58c2b37ad34503e89e78b51a50a848a0390771d84d4a70e01b","body":{"detail":"admit refuses only `GET /api/stream` and `/api/admin/shutdown` for `as: owner` (spec 2026-10-19 §2.3), but crates/clax-server/src/router.rs:548-553 also serves `GET /api/events`, `/api/artifacts/{aid}/room` and `/api/artifacts/{aid}/live` as responses that last as long as their reader, plus rmcp's `/mcp`. respond() (core.rs:503) reads a body to its end, so such a call holds a hub or room connection and buffers until the core closes or 96 MiB, and its port never hears an answer. Today's shell reaches the room by WebSocket (web/shell/src/caps/room.ts:111), not fetch, so nothing calls these yet; but a relayed fetch or a Dart call to one of them would hang silently rather than be refused.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":387},"end":{"line":407},"content_hash":"6a6801dc2a0b28236a6204abd051e1336112ecf6f08be53dd2375871175d4d08"},"suggested_fix":"Refuse the streaming routes for `call` with not_in_app (as /api/stream is), and name them in spec §2.3's table; give one a subscription path if the app comes to need it.","summary":"An owner call to one of the router's other unbounded streams (/api/events, /api/artifacts/{aid}/room, /api/artifacts/{aid}/live, GET /mcp) is admitted and never answers","tags":["review","embed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:42:06.460681Z","id":"9258d31c624db4e9e04921b5479671383ce366964755c511f37d7aeb025d5ae4","body":{"detail":"close() moves the phase to Closing before core.stop(); answer() (core.rs:448-453) selects on that change and drops the router future, so an in-flight handler is cancelled at its next await. clax serve on SIGTERM (crates/clax-server/src/serve.rs graceful shutdown) lets open requests finish for up to DRAIN_TIMEOUT (5 s) and only ends streams. A store closure already sent to the writer thread still commits, so e.g. a publish whose version row landed answers 503 `core_closed`, and what the handler would have done after its commit (hub events, wake-ups) is skipped; a caller that retries after reopening repeats the write. include/clax_embed.h:30 promises the stop of `clax serve` on SIGTERM. crates/clax-embed/tests/embed.rs:306-327 accepts 200 or 503, so the behaviour is not pinned either way.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":244},"end":{"line":264},"content_hash":"b876b8223c3451dea1471cb2f7fac64317c7a4f91ad2ba11e61db6a4b37f0eca"},"suggested_fix":"Send the core's shutdown (ending long polls and streams) first, give admitted calls a bounded drain as serve does, then cut what remains; pin it with a test that a call admitted before close answers its real status.","summary":"close cuts every call in flight at once instead of draining it as `clax serve` does, so a write that committed answers 503 core_closed","tags":["review","embed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:42:06.460722Z","id":"5f747886614fe0ae2adee9724e0497762452e0872020acf0c3d9708d1b1ae159","body":{"detail":"Core::start's progress is Store::open_reporting's callback, which hears clax_store::backfill::Progress (planning, hashing files, recording, done; crates/clax-store/src/backfill.rs:126-135). backup::before_migrate and the migrations run inside Store::open_with (crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs:260-275) with no report, so the open port hears nothing between clax_embed_open and ready/failed while a large old home is copied and migrated. Spec 2026-10-19 §2.5 step 4 says the backup and migrations report progress as {\"type\":\"opening\",\"phase\":…}, and §18 item 6 expects progress on the splash for the owner's large home.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":311},"end":{"line":322},"content_hash":"3eaf95ce95c71f21155de064ba2fe8e73484e930ae782bcfc7ecfb12ac391374"},"suggested_fix":"Give Store::open_reporting phases for the backup and each migration (or a coarse `backing up` / `migrating` pair) and post them as Opening events; test that a home with pending migrations hears them before ready.","summary":"`opening` events carry only the audit backfill's phases; the pre-migration backup and the migrations post nothing","tags":["review","embed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:42:06.460762Z","id":"f8c07f3536e96a24b2ed20373ca61d10bb3ce58d3b0619448c12e1a4f68fa820","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-embed/tests/embed.rs covers a second open in this process (OPEN, core.rs:162) but no test holds <home>/core.lock from elsewhere and expects failed `home_in_use`, which is what a second Mac app instance meets (spec 2026-10-19 §2.5 step 1), and none drives a failing migration to check failed `migration_failed` with `backup` naming the newest file under backup::dir (core.rs:333-341, newest_backup). Both are what the app shows the person instead of a connection message.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":267},"end":{"line":293},"content_hash":"6c4d0fc22960a16854d39a30c1a6ff2bafd53e3972de0c82b84df8988f754012"},"suggested_fix":"In tests/embed.rs: lock home/core.lock with std::fs::File::try_lock in the test, open, expect Failed{code:\"home_in_use\"}; and open a home whose database is at a schema the migrations refuse (a fixture as crates/clax-store/tests use) and expect migration_failed with a backup path that exists.","summary":"The cross-process `home_in_use` refusal and the `migration_failed` answer with its backup path are untested","tags":["review","tests","embed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:42:06.460802Z","id":"edbaa96d33e7ba24eb0ec597caf9eb82c1de631cc462190491e57f62f705620d","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-embed/tests/embed.rs:345-350 checks read_limited, but nothing checks that respond() maps ReadError::TooLarge to a 502 frame with code `response_too_large` (spec 2026-10-19 §2.3, §16 \"a 97 MiB response answers 502\"), nor that a body failing mid-read answers 502 response_failed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":503},"end":{"line":514},"content_hash":"95ed0e82b71914ee3224fe5058311aaf2cb0d7fd2b818161274cbc90ffb23a08"},"suggested_fix":"Make the limit a parameter of respond (RESPONSE_LIMIT in production) and test respond(res, 8) on a 9-byte body for the 502 frame and its code.","summary":"The 502 response_too_large answer is not test-pinned: only read_limited's 8/9-byte limit is","tags":["review","tests","embed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/events.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:42:06.461320Z","id":"e5573052823c2c73949fdb3f76a0aa9784b10feafe1435c5da67c695a7e58c4a","body":{"detail":"subscribe() returns silently on a core that never opened (events.rs:21-23), a refused or failed stream (:42-45, :55-57) and close (:61); ffi_subscribe answers 0 for a core whose open failed. The Dart side learns that its event port will never hear again only indirectly, from the open port's failed/closed, and a subscriber on another isolate (the worker's queue, spec §2.4) has no open port. A last message such as `event: end` (or an empty Uint8List) would let each consumer resubscribe or stop.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":17},"end":{"line":65},"content_hash":"57125be75145ee7bcfa38b29db725af6aea8919efccc585bbcd22f1efb931aed"},"summary":"A subscription that ends (core closed or failed, stream refused or errored) posts nothing to its port","tags":["review","embed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:42:06.461360Z","id":"4fa594791317130622fdb486d8691728764a4c4916477a8770ad3a1f9004b293","body":{"detail":"respond() collects the body (Bytes), frame::encode copies it into a new Vec, frame::tagged (frame.rs:91-96, called in lib.rs:140) copies that again, and Dart_PostCObject copies the typed data. For a body near RESPONSE_LIMIT (96 MiB) that is about 290 MiB of Rust allocations at once on a phone, beside the WebView's own copy.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":503},"end":{"line":533},"content_hash":"b9be6558eebd7818b1aa2547dbf571cefd75a0992ac8ac87e949395d61241e6d"},"suggested_fix":"Encode the tag, head and body into one Vec sized once (an encode_tagged(tag, head, body)), and drop the collected Bytes before posting.","summary":"A response body is copied three times in Rust before Dart copies it a fourth time","tags":["review","embed","memory","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:42:06.461401Z","id":"ba01236975a5b829dcf606ea5707e08d6c719bd23c1f03092afd0b583b04310f","body":{"detail":"request() forwards all of a content or shell-page frame's headers except those three (core.rs:471-481), so `x-clax-session`, `x-clax-via`, `origin`, `sec-fetch-*` and the like reach the router on frames that speak for a page. Spec 2026-10-19 §4.2 has the host send only Range, If-None-Match and Accept, and §2.3 says the core, not the caller, turns `as` into authority; an allowlist in the core would keep that true if a host relays more than it should.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":458},"end":{"line":500},"content_hash":"3fdaba7db8e597ffd4ed2e8dc3ccb213f416de7ba7805597558e695cd281fe8c"},"suggested_fix":"For As::Content and As::ShellPage keep only range, if-none-match, if-modified-since, accept (and service-worker, which the kill switch reads) and drop the rest.","summary":"Non-owner frames pass every header but host, authorization and cookie to the router","tags":["review","embed","security","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:42:06.461447Z","id":"caba86005749f5ba37413321461eb4217fcaf405ba7ac92733277f8b4a128c2c","body":{"detail":"Since Rust 1.81 a panic leaving an `extern \"C\"` function aborts, so there is no UB, but Embed::open's `.expect(\"the core's runtime starts\")` (core.rs:171-176) on a thread-spawn failure, or any panic in ffi_open/ffi_call before the work is spawned, kills the whole app instead of answering 0 or posting failed. A no_origins open also returns a handle that is never registered (lib.rs:86-98), so clax_embed_close on it answers 1 and its port never hears `closed`, unlike every other failed open.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":81},"end":{"line":120},"content_hash":"fcb73ef15cd49ec86da1ecb27487c74bfd6d4f71a9378cb03558ddf4b909d0fe"},"suggested_fix":"Wrap each safe half in std::panic::catch_unwind and answer 0 / 1 or post failed `internal`; register the no_origins handle (or return 0) so close behaves as for other failed opens.","summary":"The C functions' safe halves do not catch panics: a panic aborts the app's process","tags":["review","ffi","embed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:42:06.461490Z","id":"7c32aed0ae6efcfb84ee5b21b8605b881bd3ad138abb1ecf8629677e46c83ff0","body":{"detail":"Shared::release (core.rs:108-114) runs only from close() and failed(); Inner's Drop shuts the runtime down but leaves the canonical path in OPEN. The FFI registry always closes before forgetting a handle, so the app cannot hit this today, but the safe Rust API (pub Embed::open) allows it, and a test that forgets close poisons every later open of that home in its process.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":106},"end":{"line":137},"content_hash":"c179c238cfd139c3e51b0c8468532d0180a6657cd9ed1962e21809edcf8446a7"},"suggested_fix":"Release in a Drop of Shared (the lock file and the OPEN entry), keeping release()'s once-only flag.","summary":"An Embed dropped without close never leaves OPEN, so this process can never reopen that home","tags":["review","embed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/events.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:57:37.106314Z","id":"9a8a7d42c4001dae7c5864ff1c2440ee26974b0c6c51b21a7beb9ddd94c8d11e","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/transport.ts posts subscribe {id, lastEventId} since 661881d15, and spec 2026-10-19-in-process-core-design section 2.4 has the core send it as Last-Event-ID on GET /api/stream (crates/clax-server/src/routes/stream.rs reads that header). Embed::subscribe (this line) builds the request with no headers, and clax_embed_subscribe (crates/clax-embed/src/ffi.rs) has no argument for it; adding one there means a third borrowed byte slice under the unsafe exception (spec section 14). Plan Task 15 (docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-19-in-process-core.md) carries it: until then a stream the core ends starts fresh and the hub refetches on resync.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":30},"end":{"line":30},"content_hash":"b7a2704a1ca32145a4b06a1da7e1653cb63a08a9d8777d14e009a64ca3f54d88"},"summary":"Embed::subscribe and clax_embed_subscribe take no resume point: a shell document's subscribe {lastEventId} cannot yet resume the core's subscription","tags":["follow-up","revisit:Task 15 wires ChannelRelay's subscribe","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:25:01.015171Z","id":"500fc12c2c5e4cfeffa465ef52c9191c08a700b75af3f82ae1f52a17dd566938","body":{"detail":"Embed::open starts the core with require_credential: true (spec §2.3), and a shell-page frame carries no credential (spec §2.3 table; crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs request() drops authorization and cookie for it). clax_http::auth::require_credential (crates/clax-http/src/auth.rs:347-363) lets through only open_without_credential's paths (/healthz, /_clax/, /c/, /_blob/; auth.rs:332-337), so GET /a/<id>?app=1 and /assets/... as shell-page answer 401 unauthorized. Probed through Embed::call on a fresh home: '/a/<id>?app=1 -> 401 {\"error\":{\"code\":\"unauthorized\",...}}', '/_clax/bridge.js -> 200', '/c/<id>/v/1/ -> 200'. The daemon app avoided this with the clax_key_<port> cookie, which also made the shell document's boot data the owner's (shell/boot.rs assemble: who.is_owner()). Options: (a) the core adds the owner's credential to shell-page frames, since the host sends them only for the shell origin's main-frame navigation and its subresources (spec §4.2), keeping today's owner boot data; (b) open_without_credential admits /a/, /assets/ and /favicon.ico when AppState.embed is set, and the shell document's boot is a visitor's until the shell fetches over ClaxHost; (c) the core runs without require_credential, as nothing but the app can reach it (spec §4.3, no port). Phase 1's tests do not load the shell document; Tasks 14 and 15 (the scheme handlers and the host relay) need one of these.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":633},"end":{"line":646},"content_hash":"dea15ef552a3fb4864a3fe838c6576a4a852d800fdfc3d671e1c6fe5b8b35b3f"},"summary":"A shell-page frame for the shell document or its assets answers 401 under the core's require_credential, so the app's WebView cannot load the shell as spec 2026-10-19 §2.3 frames it","supersedes":"370cdcd3887110f51895282eee93acc893f02cf7243eb67dde321aa956824b5a","tags":["status:needs-decision","embed","security","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:25:40.452810Z","id":"144b8609a5b057b269096fa7287bc5d591e797365bb1984850e836c0eb172a88","body":{"detail":"Built in df7ff611c: request() (crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs:633-646) gives a shell-page frame the owner cookie (clax_http::identity::owner_cookie_name(\"localhost\") = owner_cookie_value(token)), the credential that makes Identity::owner_browser() true, so the shell document's boot data is the owner's browser's (viewer.owner true), as the daemon app's WebView was with its key cookie. A bearer token alone would pass require_credential but leave boot.viewer empty (Identity::browser_viewer reads only a browser credential). Spec §2.3's table and paragraph and §4.3 say so.","kind":"comment","references":"500fc12c2c5e4cfeffa465ef52c9191c08a700b75af3f82ae1f52a17dd566938","summary":"The owner chose option (a) on 2026-10-19: the core treats shell-page frames as the owner, since the host forwards a shell-page frame only for the shell origin's main-frame navigation and its subresources (spec 2026-10-19 §4.2) and nothing else can reach the core; content frames stay credential-free and never the owner.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:25:40.453474Z","id":"05bfd0a737b261851173c06e2f4c8cad3eecb8be861fc9f4dcf0fb117a8af665","body":{"detail":"admit (crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs:525-529) and spec 2026-10-19 §2.3's table (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md:298) admit /assets/… and /favicon.ico for shell-page frames, but the embedded web UI (clax_embedded::web_ui_paths: .vite/manifest.json, _clax/bridge.js, _clax/bridge/…, _clax/shell/…, _clax/transport.js, _clax/mark.svg, index.html, artifact.html) serves the shell's files under /_clax/, and no route serves /assets/ or /favicon.ico: as shell-page frames, now with the owner cookie, both answer the router's 404 (crates/clax-embed/tests/embed.rs the_shell_document_and_its_files_answer_a_shell_page_frame_as_the_owner pins this, and that every /_clax/ file the shell document names answers 200). Options: (a) drop both from admit and the spec, so the shell-page surface is exactly what is served; (b) keep them for a web build that adds them (a favicon in web/), and leave the 404.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":525},"end":{"line":529},"content_hash":"65b5451aa8eed23c2a538f30853ea014ad47f401599dc19600d4334db719e04b"},"summary":"Owner decision: drop /assets/ and /favicon.ico from what a shell-page frame may reach? The web UI the core serves has neither","tags":["status:needs-decision","embed","spec","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/ffi.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:32:05.163566Z","id":"29172cb235da42e8b4d50d387348a8803af7f401f82dbc4de56a8e055391cac5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b3a8beb10","summary":"Fixed in b3a8beb10: open refuses a NULL home or post (ClaxPost is Option<PostFn>) and call a NULL req, before any slice; include/clax_embed.h says so. //crates/clax-embed:nulls_test, a C program calling the exports with NULLs, passes; before the fix it aborted with 'unsafe precondition(s) violated: slice::from_raw_parts requires the pointer to be aligned and non-null'.","supersedes":"bd6b5f9640c3e876bea9f1de062e9cd505d412e37779ce4e87314bcc08d38441","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:32:05.218280Z","id":"ede42295b8004f47406eae16b3ff91d6ccf098660fac9d83f6ec82aa1d9f431f","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:388c3e77d","summary":"Fixed in 388c3e77d: close moves to Draining (new calls 503 core_closed), sends the core's shutdown, waits for calls in flight up to clax_server::serve::DRAIN_TIMEOUT, then cuts what remains and stops. Unit tests in crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs, gated by a handler that waits on a Notify (no sleeps): a_call_in_flight_at_close_answers_with_its_own_status (answered 503 before the fix, 201 now), a_call_still_running_when_the_drain_ends_answers_core_closed (drain bound 0), a_long_poll_in_flight_at_close_is_told_to_end_and_answers_200; the ambiguous close_ends_a_call_in_flight (200 or 503) is gone.","supersedes":"9258d31c624db4e9e04921b5479671383ce366964755c511f37d7aeb025d5ae4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:32:05.270398Z","id":"db25305ef750178865364f66e48d38edd48551085b1f2b66c3dfed85b797c41a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a27771d73","summary":"Fixed in a27771d73: admit refuses every route in clax_server::router::held_open (/api/stream, /api/events, /api/artifacts/{aid}/room, /api/artifacts/{aid}/live, /mcp) over call with not_in_app; guards::held_open::the_held_open_list_is_the_routers_block_and_mcp pins the list to the router's source. core::tests::each_speaker_reaches_only_its_paths failed before ('GET /api/events Owner None') and passes; tests/embed.rs no_route_that_holds_its_connection_open_is_a_call passes.","supersedes":"88445919da55cd58c2b37ad34503e89e78b51a50a848a0390771d84d4a70e01b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:32:05.320453Z","id":"6ace917ec1d15d785e5c98c163ff73a120515ca50c50e9b7110800bafb0519dc","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:88d5f406f","summary":"Fixed in 88d5f406f: Store::open_with reports Phase::BackingUp before the copy and Phase::Migrating (done of total) before each migration, and the core posts them as {\"type\":\"opening\",\"phase\":…,\"done\",\"total\"}. Passing: clax-store tests::opening_a_home_reports_each_migration_and_a_current_one_none, clax-embed opening_a_new_home_reports_each_migration_before_ready, and a_migration_that_fails_names_the_copy_made_before_it hearing 'backing up' then 'migrating'; clax serve's starting.json counts both as 'opening', as before.","supersedes":"5f747886614fe0ae2adee9724e0497762452e0872020acf0c3d9708d1b1ae159","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:32:05.423440Z","id":"33c1c2b0f7bd98b777c50d93c9688f0e24ef9f719d3997d47e3cbc49fe5d31ff","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:dded39d5d","summary":"Fixed in dded39d5d: crates/clax-embed/tests/embed.rs a_home_another_process_holds_is_in_use (the test binary re-run as a child holds core.lock; the open fails home_in_use, then the home opens once it exits) and a_migration_that_fails_names_the_copy_made_before_it (a one-page SQLite file at user_version 1; failed migration_failed with a backup path under backup::dir that exists) pass.","supersedes":"f8c07f3536e96a24b2ed20373ca61d10bb3ce58d3b0619448c12e1a4f68fa820","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:32:05.474979Z","id":"843dcda6b843631e0abf1a70c14cff68e7e7d8a9ea6a054792c9554bc266c1e3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:36ca71f1f","summary":"Fixed in 36ca71f1f: respond takes its limit; unit tests a_body_past_the_limit_answers_502_response_too_large (9 bytes over a limit of 8; 8 bytes answer 200) and a_body_that_fails_while_read_answers_502_response_failed pass.","supersedes":"edbaa96d33e7ba24eb0ec597caf9eb82c1de631cc462190491e57f62f705620d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/events.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:32:05.581427Z","id":"85b9069aad287972b9722109b2cadb8997968eadc2db90b371ee94e5ae444c77","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:859ce2a21","summary":"Fixed in 859ce2a21 and a137501b8: a subscription that ends posts `event: end` with {\"reason\":core_failed|core_closed|stream_refused|stream_ended} last (not after its subscriber said false); a handle whose open failed posts it at once. Passing: a_closed_core_ends_its_subscriptions_with_an_end_block (run 5 times), a_subscription_to_a_core_that_did_not_open_hears_only_its_end, a_subscriber_that_returns_false_hears_no_end, and ffi tests reading the end block on the subscribe port; the first two failed before.","supersedes":"e5573052823c2c73949fdb3f76a0aa9784b10feafe1435c5da67c695a7e58c4a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:32:05.634160Z","id":"2924449a227bcacce6a1bb9d92973f6d967ccbf108b0503905e6b518fd7d8768","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:810e34b53","summary":"Fixed in 810e34b53: the tag and frame head go into the posted buffer first (frame::begin, sized from the body's size hint) and each body chunk is copied in once; the request is copied once from Dart's lent buffer and its body sliced from that copy. What remains: one Rust copy each way, and postCObject's copy into the Dart heap. a_response_is_framed_after_its_tag_in_one_buffer_sized_once (capacity == len) passes.","supersedes":"4fa594791317130622fdb486d8691728764a4c4916477a8770ad3a1f9004b293","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:32:05.686911Z","id":"1dfae098dea937306d17dd527f34a20a3256294994f4ddb7d45b47d1ee7f50ab","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:cdcb83164","summary":"Fixed in cdcb83164: content and shell-page frames keep only range, if-none-match, if-modified-since, accept and service-worker (PAGE_HEADERS). a_page_frame_keeps_only_the_headers_a_scheme_request_carries failed before (x-clax-session, x-clax-via, origin, sec-fetch-site passed) and passes.","supersedes":"ba01236975a5b829dcf606ea5707e08d6c719bd23c1f03092afd0b583b04310f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:32:05.741399Z","id":"e533da925abc99e52c0e7a999a17edeb1f973dd34962f3e45acd094ac993cce9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d6b8b18ef","summary":"Fixed in d6b8b18ef: each safe half runs under catch_unwind (a panic posts failed internal, a 500 internal frame, or the end block), posts are caught too, Embed::open returns OpenError::Runtime instead of panicking, and every handle an open returns is registered (a failed one answers 503 core_failed and closes with closed). ffi tests a_failed_open_is_a_handle_that_answers_and_closes and a_post_that_panics_does_not_unwind_out_of_the_c_functions failed before and pass.","supersedes":"caba86005749f5ba37413321461eb4217fcaf405ba7ac92733277f8b4a128c2c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:32:05.792263Z","id":"6e5f73eaf70dd1d74e064b65d6172c77f4b2c6c636213df272ef533f549d58f1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:787be10b5","summary":"Fixed in 787be10b5: Shared's Drop releases the home (OPEN and core.lock). dropping_an_embed_without_close_frees_its_home failed before (the reopen answered HomeInUse) and passes.","supersedes":"7c32aed0ae6efcfb84ee5b21b8605b881bd3ad138abb1ecf8629677e46c83ff0","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:32:05.846355Z","id":"b98205c51008ef13e36c00ceaecfd81ebe0e90ebd05734bfd832ab5d19090488","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3fe892622","summary":"Fixed in 3fe892622: ffi_open logs to <home>/logs/core.log (log::path), with no new ABI; spec §2.1 says so. //crates/clax-embed:log a_core_opened_through_the_c_functions_logs_to_its_home failed before (NotFound) and passes, the log holding the core's start lines.","supersedes":"353a5bfe8ab3936b81f89d5a19b076c84ec473e51cd0908ef623dac33f2f91fb","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:32:05.897255Z","id":"d837e51378484f100dd65a51f4c9e70393ba17c1cc96f33631d76b1cc056d59b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:df7ff611c","summary":"Decided (option a, reply 144b8609) and built in df7ff611c: a shell-page frame carries the owner cookie, a content frame no credential. the_shell_document_and_its_files_answer_a_shell_page_frame_as_the_owner (GET /a/<id>?app=1 answers 200 with \"owner\":true in its boot data, and every /_clax/ file it names 200) failed before with 401 unauthorized and passes; a_page_frame_carrying_a_credential_reaches_no_api passes.","supersedes":"500fc12c2c5e4cfeffa465ef52c9191c08a700b75af3f82ae1f52a17dd566938","tags":["reason:fixed","status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:42:20.872068Z","id":"9873812c712757a6e546b106e027be47a4295ab3897d7fc6b4d78288389976dd","body":{"detail":"Embed::open spawns `opening` (core.rs:391) and close spawns its drain task (core.rs:354-385) with no catch_unwind. Tokio swallows a panic there, so Phase stays Opening (or Draining/Stopping): answer() waits on `wait_for(!Opening)` forever, Embed::ready() never resolves, close's task waits forever for the phase to leave Opening, `closed` is never posted, and Shared::release never runs while the handle is registered. include/clax_embed.h promises `port` hears ready or failed, then closed after clax_embed_close. d6b8b18ef put the C functions' safe halves and every post under catch_unwind (record e533da92) but not these two tasks, which run Core::start (store open, migrations, backfill), retire_daemon_json, newest_backup and Core::stop.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":254},"end":{"line":257},"content_hash":"56a5096d6b666d9913298045229c14aa4f9f509eba4cfdf705832296eafb8dd5"},"suggested_fix":"Run `opening` under AssertUnwindSafe(..).catch_unwind() and turn a panic into failed(&sh, \"internal\", …); run close's task the same way and, on a panic, still release the home, set Phase::Closed and emit Closed. Pin each with a test that injects a panic (a test-only hook in OpenOptions or open_draining).","summary":"A panic in the opening task or in close's task is not caught: the open port then hears neither ready/failed nor closed, calls and subscriptions wait forever, and the home stays held","tags":["review","embed","ffi","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:42:20.872129Z","id":"d62386abf4553536ae2cb7fc05e597925ee50293181f4ca379605d27d3c97e0f","body":{"detail":"810e34b53 sizes the posted buffer from the body's size hint, capped at limit + 1: `hint.exact().unwrap_or(hint.lower()).min(limit as u64 + 1)` then frame::begin. A response whose exact size is over RESPONSE_LIMIT (a large version file or asset) allocates 96 MiB + 1 bytes, copies chunks into it, and only then answers 502. On a phone that is a 96 MiB allocation for nothing. A body with no exact hint (a streamed one) starts at its lower bound (often 0) and grows by doubling, so its chunks are copied again on each regrowth, unlike the one copy the spec's §2.3 and lib.rs's module doc describe.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":684},"end":{"line":686},"content_hash":"72a8e97eb80824110d5c1f3713f46307e1e56d759592faab75bc5d706706a00c"},"suggested_fix":"Answer 502 response_too_large before reading when hint.lower() > limit; extend a_body_past_the_limit_answers_502_response_too_large with a body whose exact hint is over the limit and assert nothing near the limit is allocated (the frame's capacity). Say in §2.3 that a body of unknown size may be regrown.","summary":"respond allocates up to 96 MiB from the size hint before it reads a body it will refuse as response_too_large","tags":["review","embed","memory","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/events.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:42:20.872166Z","id":"0583b719cf1b0d27e058562d11643b160993e730050887d51aa66be0ef4473db","body":{"detail":"pump names the end by the phase when the stream ends (`ended`, events.rs:81-87, from a137501b8) but not when the router answers a non-success status: a subscribe that got Ready just before close, whose GET /api/stream reaches the store after Core::stop shut it down, answers an error and posts `event: end` with {\"reason\":\"stream_refused\"} (also the request-build failure at :67). include/clax_embed.h and spec §2.4 make core_closed the reason whenever the core closed, and a consumer that resubscribes on stream_refused would retry a closed core.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":74},"end":{"line":77},"content_hash":"a9613f6d54c99babc9304303413220498593dc9d65a65d55e5e7536c4c0bd9b9"},"suggested_fix":"Return `if phase.ready() { \"stream_refused\" } else { \"core_closed\" }` on a refusal too, as `ended` does.","summary":"A subscription whose stream request is refused because the core is closing ends with stream_refused, not core_closed","tags":["review","embed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:42:20.872807Z","id":"446adbf586b26f456900c3cd8dcb33bc9c05eae6cbde5e1bdaf9feeda54001ec","body":{"detail":"Each prefix admit lets a shell-page frame reach now carries the owner cookie (df7ff611c), so the list should be the minimum: what the embedded web UI serves (clax_embedded::web_ui_paths puts the shell's files under /_clax/) and what the shell document loads. The WebView sees the same 404 either way; with (a) it is the core's not_in_app, and a web build that adds a favicon or /assets/ fails each_speaker_reaches_only_its_paths and the shell-document test until the path is admitted on purpose, with its credential decided. each_speaker_reaches_only_its_paths (core.rs) asserts HEAD /assets/x.js and GET /favicon.ico are admitted; both flip to refused. The same pass should settle spec §4.2's shell documents (line 429: `/`, `/inbox`, `/people`, `/a/…`), since admit refuses `/` for shell-page (asserted in the same test): either the app loads only /a/… and §4.2 says so, or admit adds them.","kind":"comment","references":"05bfd0a737b261851173c06e2f4c8cad3eecb8be861fc9f4dcf0fb117a8af665","summary":"Recommend (a): drop /assets/ and /favicon.ico from admit and from spec §2.3's table, so a shell-page frame reaches exactly the paths the core serves and the shell loads","tags":["review","embed","spec","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:21:47.890305Z","id":"3fec89576515d983c2707b431513daa0d9ad9e17d0a49a0f64904cb3d7e71f85","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:16748225b","summary":"Fixed in 16748225b: Embed::open runs its opening task under catch_unwind (a panic posts failed code internal and releases the home), and Embed::close runs its drain and stop the same way (a panic still cuts calls, stops a core left, releases the home and posts closed). Evidence: core::tests::a_panic_while_opening_fails_the_open_and_frees_the_home and a_panic_while_closing_still_closes_and_frees_the_home, which timed out (60 s) before the fix and pass after; bazelisk test --keep_going //crates/clax-embed:all //crates/clax-server:all //crates/clax-http:all //crates/clax-store:all //scripts:no_unsafe //scripts:no_unsafe_test //scripts:crate_layers at 817e9401b: 19 tests pass.","supersedes":"9873812c712757a6e546b106e027be47a4295ab3897d7fc6b4d78288389976dd","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/events.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:21:48.257311Z","id":"9cd63d8f195da055970a87768451d15d2364fb0ce9e82896b1b0d5bd63f1cb85","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:db9ffb89e","summary":"Fixed in db9ffb89e: pump names a refused stream core_closed when the core is no longer ready, as it does an ended one. Evidence: core::tests::a_stream_refused_because_the_core_is_closing_ends_core_closed failed before (end reason stream_refused) and passes; bazelisk test --keep_going //crates/clax-embed:all //crates/clax-server:all //crates/clax-http:all //crates/clax-store:all //scripts:no_unsafe //scripts:no_unsafe_test //scripts:crate_layers at 817e9401b: 19 tests pass.","supersedes":"0583b719cf1b0d27e058562d11643b160993e730050887d51aa66be0ef4473db","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:21:49.296150Z","id":"c39c24a0f2e42da91747a3e21cc7d699cfa636ff363c1a289fedaba1599b2813","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:135f99f50","summary":"Fixed in 135f99f50: respond answers 502 response_too_large before reading when the size hint's lower bound is past the limit, and sizes the buffer from the hint capped at the limit; lib.rs and spec §2.3 say a body of unknown size may grow it. Evidence: core::tests::a_body_whose_size_is_known_past_the_limit_is_refused_unread (a Limited body whose read is observable) answered response_failed before and passes; bazelisk test --keep_going //crates/clax-embed:all //crates/clax-server:all //crates/clax-http:all //crates/clax-store:all //scripts:no_unsafe //scripts:no_unsafe_test //scripts:crate_layers at 817e9401b: 19 tests pass.","supersedes":"d62386abf4553536ae2cb7fc05e597925ee50293181f4ca379605d27d3c97e0f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:21:49.480138Z","id":"c3e8faa0c6368ae8f84b860f37f3ec8c40ecde89554a630634c33f042df3eed5","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"05bfd0a737b261851173c06e2f4c8cad3eecb8be861fc9f4dcf0fb117a8af665","summary":"Owner decision (2026-10-19): option (a). Drop /assets/ and /favicon.ico from admit and from spec §2.3's table; the app loads no gallery documents, so §4.2 names /a/<id> as the only shell document in the app.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-embed/src/core.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:21:49.480481Z","id":"47deeae91578d387048c24de27aa2d15abfc63212ad7bcba502b051fe3be2a19","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:8118e661c","summary":"Done in 8118e661c as the owner decided: admit lets a shell-page frame reach /a/, /_clax/, /c/ and /_blob/ only; §2.3's table and §4.2 match. Evidence: core::tests::each_speaker_reaches_only_its_paths, with HEAD /assets/x.js and GET /favicon.ico flipped to refused, failed before the change and passes; embed.rs the_shell_document_and_its_files_answer_a_shell_page_frame_as_the_owner asserts both answer not_in_app; bazelisk test --keep_going //crates/clax-embed:all //crates/clax-server:all //crates/clax-http:all //crates/clax-store:all //scripts:no_unsafe //scripts:no_unsafe_test //scripts:crate_layers at 817e9401b: 19 tests pass.","supersedes":"05bfd0a737b261851173c06e2f4c8cad3eecb8be861fc9f4dcf0fb117a8af665","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
